.TH WEBDAV-SERVER 1 "September 2026" "Qore XML" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
webdav-server \- serve a directory over WebDAV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B webdav-server
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start a WebDAV HTTP server using the Qore filesystem handler.
By default, serve a temporary directory on an automatically assigned port.
The server reports its root and listening port unless quiet mode is enabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep the temporary directory after exit. Ignored with an explicit root.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port= PORT
Listen on PORT; zero selects an available port.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress console logging.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root= DIRECTORY
Serve an existing directory instead of a temporary directory.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP, SIGUSR1 and SIGUSR2 stop the server gracefully.
.SH NOTES
The example server has no authentication and accepts writes.
Use it only on a trusted network with an appropriate directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore (1)
